course: dictionary
lesson: 9381
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them show you which meaning the writer wants. «Spotted» is one of these words. It can describe a thing covered with spots, or it can be the past form of «spot», which means to notice something.
explain: «Spotted hyenas have some of the strongest bites of any mammal.» Here spotted is an adjective. It describes the hyenas and tells you what their coats look like: covered with spots. Try the swap: the sentence still makes sense with the word «spotty» in its place, so spotted is describing something.
explain: «Mia spotted the missing key under the sofa.» Here spotted is a verb in the past tense. Mia did not paint spots on the key. She noticed it. Swap in «noticed»: «Mia noticed the missing key under the sofa.» It still makes sense, so this spotted means noticed.
fact: Spotted can describe something covered with spots or dots, such as «a spotted dog».
fact: As the past form of «spot», spotted means noticed or seen, especially something that was hard to find.
fact: The verb «spot» has four forms: spot, spots, spotted, spotting.
fact: «Spotted hyenas» get their name from the spots on their coats.
fact: «Spotted the difference» means you noticed what was different between two pictures.
exercise: «The spotted dog wagged its tail.» What does spotted mean here? | Noticed | Lost | *Covered with spots | Hungry
exercise: «Mo spotted the missing key under the sofa.» What does spotted mean here? | Covered with spots | Broken | Given away | *Noticed or saw
exercise: Which is the past form of the verb spot? | spotting | *spotted | spot | spots
test: Ruby read «a spotted leopard» in her book, then said, «I spotted a clue under the table!» Which meaning fits the second sentence? | *Noticed a clue | Fell over | Covered in spots | Ran fast
test: Which sentence uses spotted to describe a thing, not as a verb? | *«The spotted hyena has a strong bite.» | «They spotted the cat.» | «She spotted the difference.» | «He spotted a bird on the fence.»
exam: «The spotted hyena whooped to call its clan.» What does spotted describe in this sentence? | The sound of the whoop | *The hyena, which is covered with spots | A clue that someone found | A bone it crushed
